            "reason": "The public FT_StreamRec shape advertises one byte while both base and read are null. Pinned ftbzip2.c would pass this unsafe record into FT_Stream_ReadAt and dereference null; the maintained C oracle therefore records the safe wrapper-boundary Invalid_Stream_Handle result without invoking undefined behavior, while Rust, C ABI, and WASM must reject before materialization.",
